BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  In the dawn of the world, two spirits, Aethel and Vora, stood upon the bridge of stardust. Aet) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    hel held five embers of pure light. He could hoard them, keeping the warmth for his own cold) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (     shadow, or he could cast them into the void toward Vora. Aethel knew the ancient law of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (     bridge: what he sent would bloom into three times its strength upon arrival.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  Vora waited on the far side. She held the power to snuff the light or to return a portion, kee) Tj ET
