BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  In the beginning, there were two spirits: Aethel, the Keeper of Seeds, and Solon, the Keeper o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    f Streams. They lived on opposite sides of a vast, barren canyon. Aethel possessed five gold) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    en seeds, but the soil on her side was salt and stone. Solon lived by a river, but his land ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    was barren of life.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  Across the void, they watched each other. Aethel understood that if she hoarded her seeds, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    y would remain dormant, useless jewels. She cast them across the abyss, trusting the wind. S) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    olon caught them, his hands wet with the river's bounty. Had he kept the seeds, he would hav) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    e possessed only grain; had he returned nothing, he would have remained a wanderer in a dese) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    rt. Instead, he infused the seeds with the essence of the river, tripling their vitality, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    d cast the harvest back across the canyon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  Trust became the bridge. Because Aethel risked her store and Solon honored the gift by nurturi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    ng it, the canyon floor bloomed into an emerald paradise. They learned that true wealth is n) Tj ET
