BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (  In the beginning, the Weaver and the Harvester stood on opposite banks of a wide, silent river) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    . The Harvester held a handful of golden seeds, but the soil on his side was cracked and bar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    ren. The Weaver possessed a loom of infinite capacity, yet she had no thread to weave.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  The Oracle whispered a truth: "To hoard is to wither; to release is to flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  Hesitantly, the Harvester cast his seeds across the rushing water. The Weaver caught them, and) Tj ET
