BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    ngth. The Weaver, recognizing the origins of her newfound wealth, returned a generous portio) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    n to the Harvester. With these threads, the Harvester stitched a bridge across the river, un) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    iting them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  They realized the river was not a barrier but a mechanism of growth. When seeds were held, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    y remained mere grains, but when offered in faith, they became tapestries of prosperity. Thu) Tj ET
