BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  In the dawn of the world, two spirits, Sol and Luna, stood upon a barren plain. Sol held five ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    golden grains of light, the foundation of existence. Alone, Sol could do little with these g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    rains. Luna held the fertile soil of the earth, waiting for a catalyst to bring forth life. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    Sol stepped forward and offered all five grains to Luna. When Luna received them, the offeri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ng grew threefold, shimmering with the potential of a thousand harvests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  Luna understood the weight of this gift. She could have buried the grains deep in the shadows,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (     keeping the wealth for herself, leaving the plains in eternal twilight. Instead, she chose ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    to nurture the light. She returned a portion of the harvest back to Sol, ensuring they both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    thrived in the newfound warmth. This cycle of offering and return transformed the barren pla) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    in into a garden of emerald and gold. They learned that wealth is not in possession, but in ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    the flow of trust. When one risks everything to share, and the other honors that risk with f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    airness, the world blooms. Thus, the law of the harvest was written: he who sows with faith ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    shall reap in abundance, provided the hand that receives knows how to give back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
