BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    o the shore of the Keeper. The Keeper stood before fifteen seeds. He could hoard them, buryi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    ng them in the cold clay to wither, or he could return a portion, planting the seeds in the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    garden between them. When the Keeper returned a generous share, the Giver realized the magic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (     wasn't in the seeds, but in the exchange. Together, they grew a grove that fed the land, pr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    oving that wealth, when hoarded, remains static, but when shared, blooms into abundance. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (     game of the spirits defines the cycle of life: send to sow, return to reap, and trust to gr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ow. For in their quiet arrangement, the forest flourished, and the spirits learned that to h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    old everything is to possess nothing, while to share is to multiply the very essence of thei) Tj ET
