BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      In the beginning, there were two spirits: Aethel, the Keeper of Seeds, and Solon, the Keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        er of Streams. They lived on opposite sides of a vast, barren canyon. Aethel possessed f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        ive golden seeds, but the soil on her side was salt and stone. Solon lived by a river, b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        ut his land was barren of life.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      Across the void, they watched each other. Aethel understood that if she hoarded her seeds,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (         they would remain dormant, useless jewels. She cast them across the abyss, trusting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (         wind. Solon caught them, his hands wet with the river's bounty. Had he kept the seeds, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        he would have possessed only grain; had he returned nothing, he would have remained a wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        nderer in a desert. Instead, he infused the seeds with the essence of the river, triplin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        g their vitality, and cast the harvest back across the canyon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      Trust became the bridge. Because Aethel risked her store and Solon honored the gift by nur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        turing it, the canyon floor bloomed into an emerald paradise. They learned that true wea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        lth is not what one holds in a closed palm, but what is shared and multiplied through th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        e courage of an open hand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
