BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      In the dawn of the world, two spirits, Sol and Luna, stood upon a barren plain. Sol held f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ive golden grains of light, the foundation of existence. Alone, Sol could do little with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (         these grains. Luna held the fertile soil of the earth, waiting for a catalyst to bring ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        forth life. Sol stepped forward and offered all five grains to Luna. When Luna received ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        them, the offering grew threefold, shimmering with the potential of a thousand harvests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      Luna understood the weight of this gift. She could have buried the grains deep in the shad) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        ows, keeping the wealth for herself, leaving the plains in eternal twilight. Instead, sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        e chose to nurture the light. She returned a portion of the harvest back to Sol, ensurin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        g they both thrived in the newfound warmth. This cycle of offering and return transforme) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        d the barren plain into a garden of emerald and gold. They learned that wealth is not in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         possession, but in the flow of trust. When one risks everything to share, and the other) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         honors that risk with fairness, the world blooms. Thus, the law of the harvest was writ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        ten: he who sows with faith shall reap in abundance, provided the hand that receives kno) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        ws how to give back.) Tj ET
