BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      In the dawn of the First Age, the Sun and the Moon were bound by an ancient pact. The Sun,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         overflowing with golden radiance, held five embers of creation. Seeking to brighten the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (         void, the Sun cast its warmth toward the Moon, empowering it three times over. The Moon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (         stood at the precipice of existence, holding the Sun's gift. If the Moon clutched the l) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ight for itself, the embers would fade, and the universe would succumb to cold, stagnant) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (         shadow. But the Moon understood the rhythm of sacrifice; it gathered the light and retu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        rned a portion, not to hoard, but to weave a cycle of perpetual harmony.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      When the Moon returned the light, the Sun grew brighter, and the two danced in a celestial) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         exchange. Their shared burden became a bridge, turning the void into a tapestry of star) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        s. Those who sought to take without giving found their own light extinguished, for the u) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        niverse does not favor the isolated. To play the game of existence is to trust in the re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        turn, for the gold we release is not lost, but transformed into the harmony that sustain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        s us all. In the reflection of the Moon, the Sun sees the truth: prosperity is built on ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        shared embers.) Tj ET
