BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      Myth: In the Weaver's chamber, threads of silver and gold hung suspended in the stillness ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        of the loom. The Weaver held five strands of pure potential, knowing that to keep them c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        oiled was to deny the tapestry its pattern. She cast them forth into the void, where the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        y were spun by the cosmic tension into fifteen strands of shimmering light. The Receiver) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        , watching the threads arrive, understood the fragile balance of the warp and weft. If s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        he pulled too hard, the pattern would tear; if she let go entirely, the threads would sc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        atter. Instead, she knotted the strands with deliberate grace, weaving them back into a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        design that returned half, honoring the origin point of the silk. This design was not st) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        atic but a growing fabric of interconnected destiny. Every cycle of the loom added a lay) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        er of strength to the whole. They understood that the game was not a depletion of resour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ces but a weaving of a common future. By returning what was due, the Receiver ensured th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        e Weaver would cast again, and by casting again, the Weaver ensured the tapestry would n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        ever unravel. In the endless weaving, they found that trust is the strongest material, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        nd reciprocity is the stitch that binds the stars.) Tj ET
